The `executeModule` method takes a module function and arguments as arguments and returns a promise that resolves to the result of executing the module with the given arguments. The `executeModuleWithErrorHandling` method is similar, but it also handles errors by logging them to the console and returning null.

The `loadAndExecuteModule` method takes a module name and arguments as arguments and returns a promise that resolves to the result of loading and executing the module with the given arguments. The `loadAndExecuteModules` method takes an array of module names and arguments as arguments and returns a promise that resolves to an array of results from loading and executing each module.

The code also includes an example usage section that demonstrates how to use the `moduleLoader` object to load and execute multiple modules with given arguments."]

