The `AddRange` method is used to add a new random number generator to the dictionary of generators, along with its minimum and maximum values. If the specified ID already exists in the dictionary, the existing generator is replaced with the new one. The `GenerateRandomInteger` and `GenerateRandomFloat` methods are used to generate random integers and floats within the specified range for a given generator ID. If an invalid generator ID is provided, an `ArgumentException` is thrown.

The `ResetAllGenerators` method resets all generators to their initial state by calling the `Reset` method on each one. This ensures that the generators are in a known state and can be used again without any issues.

Finally, the `ToString` method overrides the default behavior of the `Object.ToString` method and returns a string representation of the current range settings for each generator. This is useful for debugging purposes or when displaying the status of the generators to the user.']

