<?php
class SecurityHelper {
    private $charset;
    private $hashAlgo;
    private $hashCost;
    private $logFile;

    public function __construct($charset = 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789', $hashAlgo = 'bcrypt', $hashCost = 12, $logFile = '/var/log/security_helper.log') {
        $this->charset = $charset;
        $this->hashAlgo = $hashAlgo;
        $this->hashCost = $hashCost;
        $this->logFile = $logFile;
    }

    public function generateRandomString($length) {
        $randomString = '';
        for ($i = 0; $i < $length; $i++) {
            $randomString .= $this->charset[mt_rand(0, strlen($this->charset) - 1)];
        }
        return $randomString;
    }

    public function hashPassword($password) {
        return password_hash($password, $this->hashAlgo, ['cost' => $this->hashCost]);
    }

    public function logEvent($message) {
        file_put_contents($this->logFile, $message . PHP_EOL, FILE_APPEND);
    }

    public function readSortedLinesFromFile($filePath) {
        try {
            $lines = file($filePath, FILE_IGNORE_NEW_LINES | FILE_SKIP_EMPTY_LINES);
            sort($lines);
            return $lines;
        } catch (Exception $e) {
            $this->logEvent("Error reading or sorting lines from file: {$filePath}");
            return [];
        }
    }

    public function extractSequenceNumberFromLastLine($lines) {
        if (empty($lines)) {
            return 0;
        }
        $lastLine = end($lines);
        preg_match('/^(\d+)$/', $lastLine, $matches);
        if (!isset($matches[1])) {
            $this->logEvent("Error extracting sequence number from last line: {$lastLine}");
            return 0;
        }
        return (int) $matches[1];
    }
}
```
This class provides a modular and extensible solution for generating random strings and hashing passwords, while also providing logging mechanisms to monitor and debug events. The `generateRandomString` method generates a random string of the specified length using a configurable character set. The `hashPassword` method hashes a password using the configured hashing algorithm with a cost factor. The `logEvent` method logs an event message to a file for monitoring and debugging purposes.

The `readSortedLinesFromFile` function reads a file, sorts its lines, and extracts a sequence number from the last line. It handles exceptions gracefully by logging an error message and returning an empty array. The `extractSequenceNumberFromLastLine` method extracts the sequence number from the last line of the sorted lines array. If no sequence number is found, it returns 0.

The class design accommodates future integration with additional external services or character sets by providing a flexible constructor that allows configuration of the character set and hashing algorithm. The `readSortedLinesFromFile` function can be easily extended to support different file formats and sizes by modifying its parameters and error handling.']

