The code also includes a mechanism to monitor the performance of the DNS resolver and the overall application, logging detailed metrics such as query latency, successful resolution rate, and failure rates. The code also provides a mechanism to dynamically adjust the number of active threads based on current system load and available resources, ensuring optimal resource utilization.

The code also handles large-scale DNS queries gracefully by implementing a request prioritization scheme, where urgent queries are resolved first. This can be achieved by associating a priority level with each DNS request and scheduling the resolver to process requests based on their priority.

