The code includes robust error checking for invalid input, such as non-numeric ports, excessively large sizes, and malformed IP formats. It also handles concurrent modifications to device connections and status flags without causing data corruption. The code ensures that the implementation gracefully manages edge cases, such as attempting to access or modify out-of-bounds elements, and properly frees all allocated memory before the function exits.

