The `mempool_alloc` function first checks if the requested size is within the bounds of the pool, then calculates the aligned size and alignment requirements for the memory block. It then checks if there is enough memory available in the pool to allocate the requested amount of memory, and allocates the memory block from the pool if there is enough space. Finally, it returns a pointer to the allocated memory block.

The `mempool_free` function first checks if the data pointer is within the bounds of the pool, then calculates the offset of the memory block from the start of the pool. If the memory block is still in use, it updates the used memory counter and returns. Otherwise, it does nothing.

