The function uses dynamic memory allocation to allocate memory for the resource bundle and its items. It supports multiple file formats, including JSON and CSV, with different parsing strategies for each format. The function also implements a mechanism to detect and report malformed data within the file, including mismatched brackets, incorrect delimiters, and inconsistent data types.

The function is thread-safe and handles memory allocation failures gracefully by logging appropriate error messages and returning an error code. It is well-documented and includes detailed logging for debugging purposes. The function also supports dynamic updates to the configuration, allowing some parameters to be changed without reinitializing the entire configuration structure.']

