The function also includes unit tests and integration tests to validate its behavior under various conditions, including edge cases and system integration tests with an external data management system (DMS). The unit tests cover the basic functionality of the function, while the integration tests simulate high-load scenarios and varying load conditions to ensure the function's robustness and performance.

The code also includes a caching mechanism to reduce frequent interactions with the DMS and improve response times. This mechanism allows the function to maintain consistency in its behavior even under unexpected changes in DMS availability or data transmission rates.

