The function `create_projects` takes an integer argument `num_projects` that represents the number of projects to be created. It checks if the number is valid (positive) and allocates memory for an array of `project` structures using `malloc`. It initializes each project in the array with a null pointer for the name, deadline, priority level, and status.

The function `update_project_status` takes a pointer to a `project` structure and a string argument representing the new status as input. It checks if the project is valid and updates the status of the project by freeing the existing status string and allocating memory for the new one using `malloc`.

The function `update_project_deadline` takes a pointer to a `project` structure and two integer arguments representing the month and day as input. It checks if the project is valid and updates the deadline of the project by assigning the new values to the corresponding fields.

The function `print_project` takes a pointer to a `project` structure as input and prints its details in a formatted manner using `printf`.

The function `print_projects` takes an array of pointers to `project` structures and an integer argument representing the number of projects as input. It checks if the number is valid (positive) and prints the details of each project in the array using `print_project`.

The function `free_projects` takes an array of pointers to `project` structures and an integer argument representing the number of projects as input. It checks if the number is valid (positive) and frees memory allocated for each project in the array using `free`, then frees memory allocated for the array itself using `free`.

