The code also defines a function to serialize the telemetry data into JSON format and store it in a memory-mapped file specified by a user-provided filename. It efficiently allocates and deallocates memory, handles errors gracefully, and adheres to strict performance constraints. The function supports dynamic reconfiguration of the shared data structure at runtime without losing existing data and allows for efficient updates to the sensor network based on new measurement types and default values.

The code also supports versioned JSON serialization to accommodate future changes while maintaining backward compatibility. It handles potential race conditions when writing to the filesystem and ensures the function is efficient and scalable under high-concurrency scenarios.']

