["```php
<?php

class UtilityHelper {
    private $charset;
    private $hashAlgo;
    private $hashCost;
    private $logFile;

    public function __construct($charset = 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789', $hashAlgo = 'bcrypt', $hashCost = 12, $logFile = '/var/log/utility_helper.log') {
        $this->charset = $charset;
        $this->hashAlgo = $hashAlgo;
        $this->hashCost = $hashCost;
        $this->logFile = $logFile;
    }

    public function generateRandomString($length) {
        return substr(str_shuffle($this->charset), 0, $length);
    }

    public function hashPassword($password) {
        return password_hash($password, $this->hashAlgo, ['cost' => $this->hashCost]);
    }

    public function readFileAndExtractSequenceNumber($filePath) {
        $lines = file($filePath);
        sort($lines);
        $lastLine = end($lines);
        return explode(' ', $lastLine)[0];
    }

    private function logEvent($message, $level = 'info') {
        if ($this->logFile) {
            file_put_contents($this->logFile, date('Y-m-d H:i:s') . ' - ' . $level . ' - ' . $message . PHP_EOL, FILE_APPEND);
        }
    }
}
```
This class provides several utility functions for a high-traffic web application. The `generateRandomString` method generates random strings of a specified length using a configurable character set. The `hashPassword` method securely hashes passwords for user authentication using the bcrypt algorithm with a cost factor of 12. The `readFileAndExtractSequenceNumber` method reads a file, sorts its lines, and extracts a sequence number from the last line.

The class also includes logging mechanisms to record all events for monitoring and debugging purposes. The `logEvent` method writes log messages to a specified file path.

To support extensibility, the class design accommodates future integration with additional external services or character sets. Developers can make trade-offs between efficiency, usability, maintainability, and scalability, ensuring that the class can adapt to changing requirements without significant refactoring. Implementations should be robust, handling various file formats and sizes gracefully, and minimizing the risk of performance degradation under stress conditions."]

